# jemdoc: menu{MENU}{software.html}
= Software

== HKU ECE Passivity-Based Stability Workbench

*Yongheng Wang, Xiemin Mo, and Tao Liu*. Version 3.0, 2026.

A MATLAB/MATPOWER research prototype for decentralized passivity-based small-signal stability screening and local virtual-shunt passivation of converter-dominated power systems. The package provides a graphical workbench, a numerical backend, and a reproducible IEEE 39-bus no-grounding case study.

\[[static/software/HKU_ECE_PassivityWorkbench_v3.0.zip Download]\]
\[[https://github.com/HKUYonghengWang/HKU-ECE-Passivity-Based-Stability-Workbench Code]\]
\[[https://github.com/HKUYonghengWang/HKU-ECE-Passivity-Based-Stability-Workbench/blob/main/CITATION.cff Citation]\]
\[[https://github.com/HKUYonghengWang/HKU-ECE-Passivity-Based-Stability-Workbench/blob/main/LICENSE.txt License]\]

*Requirements.* MATLAB R2022b or newer is recommended; MATPOWER and Control System Toolbox are required.

*Main files.*
- launch_hku_passivity_workbench.m: GUI launcher.
- src/HKU_ECE_PassivityWorkbenchApp.m: MATLAB app.
- src/hku_passivity_engine.m: numerical backend.
- demo/hku_case39_no_ground_demo.m: paper-style IEEE 39-bus demo.
- examples/run_case39_no_ground_demo.m: minimal demo runner.

*Quick start.*
~~~
{}{code}
addpath(genpath('path_to_matpower'));
addpath('path_to/HKU_ECE_PassivityWorkbench_v3.0');
launch_hku_passivity_workbench
~~~

*Recommended citation.* If you use this software, please cite the associated passivity-based decentralized stability study and the software metadata in CITATION.cff.
